WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.180 --> 00:00:03.240
- It's open, flipped closed.

00:00:03.240 --> 00:00:06.157
(phone slaps shut)

00:00:07.330 --> 00:00:08.406
This is the Moto Razr haptic sounds.

00:00:08.406 --> 00:00:11.323
(phone slaps shut)

00:00:15.218 --> 00:00:17.718
(phone rings)

00:00:18.880 --> 00:00:21.030
I've been here now for about three hours

00:00:21.030 --> 00:00:25.080
trying to make a musical
review with flip phone sounds

00:00:25.080 --> 00:00:27.414
because the sound is awesome,
and it brings me back

00:00:27.414 --> 00:00:31.286
to my younger years,
and now, here in 2020,

00:00:31.286 --> 00:00:33.380
the flip is back.

00:00:33.380 --> 00:00:35.345
The new $1,500 Moto Razr,

00:00:35.345 --> 00:00:39.897
and the $1,380 Samsung
Galaxy Z Flip have classic

00:00:39.897 --> 00:00:43.470
clamshell designs, so I
hired a music producer,

00:00:43.470 --> 00:00:45.631
Ben Walding, to see if we
could do a musical review

00:00:45.631 --> 00:00:47.727
with just the sounds of flip phones.

00:00:47.727 --> 00:00:49.030
Can we do it?

00:00:49.030 --> 00:00:50.376
- Absolutely.

00:00:50.376 --> 00:00:51.209
- He says so.

00:00:57.920 --> 00:00:59.210
You hear that creak?

00:00:59.210 --> 00:01:00.043
- Yeah, yeah, yeah.

00:01:00.043 --> 00:01:01.550
Get just one more.

00:01:01.550 --> 00:01:04.160
- Neither phone is as
easy to open with one hand

00:01:04.160 --> 00:01:05.263
as the original Razr.

00:01:06.223 --> 00:01:08.660
(phone hits floor)

00:01:08.660 --> 00:01:10.660
It takes a little skill and muscle.

00:01:10.660 --> 00:01:12.689
Put your finger under there.

00:01:12.689 --> 00:01:14.440
The Razr is definitely easier
than the Flip Z to open

00:01:14.440 --> 00:01:15.580
with one hand though.

00:01:15.580 --> 00:01:17.313
The Samsung Z Flip.

00:01:18.790 --> 00:01:21.230
But the Razr feels much flimsier to flip

00:01:21.230 --> 00:01:22.900
because of its hinge.

00:01:22.900 --> 00:01:27.230
You can hear this as it opens and closes,

00:01:27.230 --> 00:01:31.200
plus, you can see the screen
rise up right there, and bend.

00:01:31.200 --> 00:01:33.450
Don't you worry about this, says Motorola.

00:01:33.450 --> 00:01:35.809
The sound is intrinsic to
the mechanical movement

00:01:35.809 --> 00:01:37.360
of the phone.

00:01:37.360 --> 00:01:40.031
Razr has undergone rigorous
durability testing,

00:01:40.031 --> 00:01:41.931
and the reported sounds in no way affect

00:01:41.931 --> 00:01:44.130
the quality of the product.

00:01:44.130 --> 00:01:45.479
One sound you won't mind...

00:01:45.479 --> 00:01:46.890
(phone slaps shut)

00:01:46.890 --> 00:01:49.080
Boom, it's very satisfying,

00:01:49.080 --> 00:01:51.010
even more than the Z Flip.

00:01:51.010 --> 00:01:53.323
The Z Flip's hideaway
hinge, as Samsung calls it

00:01:53.323 --> 00:01:55.550
feels more solid.

00:01:55.550 --> 00:01:57.045
Hear anything?

00:01:57.045 --> 00:01:57.955
- No, I can't even hear that.

00:01:57.955 --> 00:01:58.788
- [Joanna] Can't hear it, no.

00:01:58.788 --> 00:01:59.621
- Even I can't hear it.

00:01:59.621 --> 00:02:01.890
- So rigid, and so sturdy.

00:02:01.890 --> 00:02:03.984
Now, for the foldable screens themselves.

00:02:03.984 --> 00:02:07.954
This is the Moto Razr screen tapping.

00:02:07.954 --> 00:02:09.970
(Joanna taps screen)

00:02:09.970 --> 00:02:12.867
The Moto Razr has a
6.2-inch foldable polymer

00:02:12.867 --> 00:02:15.590
that is plastic screen.

00:02:15.590 --> 00:02:17.513
It feels very thin, so
you can actually hear,

00:02:17.513 --> 00:02:21.800
in some areas, the screen
hitting the surface behind it.

00:02:21.800 --> 00:02:24.890
You can also see outlines
of what's under there.

00:02:24.890 --> 00:02:26.977
Because it's plastic, the
screen can also be easily

00:02:26.977 --> 00:02:28.980
dented, or scratched.

00:02:28.980 --> 00:02:32.048
The Samsung Z Flip, on the
other hand, has a 6.7-inch

00:02:32.048 --> 00:02:34.705
foldable screen, with a layer of plastic,

00:02:34.705 --> 00:02:36.770
and a layer of glass.

00:02:36.770 --> 00:02:39.640
How Samsung's folding glass, it won't say.

00:02:39.640 --> 00:02:41.860
Regardless, the screen feels a lot firmer

00:02:41.860 --> 00:02:43.180
than the Razr.

00:02:43.180 --> 00:02:45.270
That said, it still
comes with a whole bunch

00:02:45.270 --> 00:02:48.310
of warnings about how easily
the screen can be damaged.

00:02:48.310 --> 00:02:50.612
There is this crease here,
but Samsung's playing that up,

00:02:50.612 --> 00:02:54.390
creating software that
splits the screen in half.

00:02:54.390 --> 00:02:56.200
Look, a mini laptop.

00:02:56.200 --> 00:02:58.900
The Razr's outside
screen is great, though.

00:02:58.900 --> 00:03:00.010
I love keeping it closed,

00:03:00.010 --> 00:03:02.330
and just glancing at notifications.

00:03:02.330 --> 00:03:05.270
The Z Flip's outside
screen is just too tiny.

00:03:05.270 --> 00:03:06.689
All right, let's hear it.

00:03:06.689 --> 00:03:07.680
- Here it comes.

00:03:07.680 --> 00:03:09.660
- The Flip is back.

00:03:09.660 --> 00:03:10.945
You can hear this creak.

00:03:10.945 --> 00:03:12.925
You hear it?

00:03:12.925 --> 00:03:14.860
And crinkle.

00:03:14.860 --> 00:03:16.800
Nice, I love it.

00:03:16.800 --> 00:03:18.320
Okay, we're gonna move
on to the second section

00:03:18.320 --> 00:03:20.400
of the song, which I
want to be about the why.

00:03:20.400 --> 00:03:23.020
Why would you get a flip phone today?

00:03:23.020 --> 00:03:24.870
One word, compact.

00:03:24.870 --> 00:03:27.830
Both phones are so much smaller
than a regular smartphone

00:03:27.830 --> 00:03:30.543
when you fold them up, and
there's another reason.

00:03:31.380 --> 00:03:34.470
Remember when flip phones
were actual phones?

00:03:34.470 --> 00:03:36.540
This feels more like a phone, phone,

00:03:36.540 --> 00:03:39.100
and the call quality's been good, too.

00:03:39.100 --> 00:03:41.117
Why does nobody pick up the phone anymore?

00:03:41.117 --> 00:03:42.040
- [Woman] Hello.

00:03:42.040 --> 00:03:45.320
- And boom, you can just
hang up with a flip.

00:03:45.320 --> 00:03:46.800
Big points for Motorola here.

00:03:46.800 --> 00:03:49.234
It also has this retro
Razr keypad with sounds

00:03:49.234 --> 00:03:50.581
of the original Razr.

00:03:50.581 --> 00:03:51.414
(phone rings)

00:03:51.414 --> 00:03:52.785
- [Announcer] Hello Moto.

00:03:52.785 --> 00:03:55.340
(phone rings)

00:03:55.340 --> 00:03:56.354
- What you got so far?

00:03:56.354 --> 00:03:57.466
- Check it out.

00:03:57.466 --> 00:03:58.312
(phone rings)

00:03:58.312 --> 00:03:59.381
- Why does nobody pick
up the phone anymore?

00:03:59.381 --> 00:04:00.515
(phone slaps shut)

00:04:00.515 --> 00:04:01.410
- Hello?

00:04:01.410 --> 00:04:02.520
(phone slaps shut)

00:04:02.520 --> 00:04:03.852
- Why do you need a flip anyway?

00:04:03.852 --> 00:04:05.790
(phone slaps shut)

00:04:05.790 --> 00:04:07.140
Phones are now too big.

00:04:07.140 --> 00:04:08.770
I love section two.

00:04:08.770 --> 00:04:11.104
Now, section three needs
to have everything else

00:04:11.104 --> 00:04:13.312
that people wanna know about this phone,

00:04:13.312 --> 00:04:14.970
like the camera.

00:04:14.970 --> 00:04:17.490
The Razr camera is bad.

00:04:17.490 --> 00:04:19.558
Not only does it take bad
pictures, but the shutter's

00:04:19.558 --> 00:04:22.770
so slow, you often miss your shot.

00:04:22.770 --> 00:04:24.780
The battery life, not good either.

00:04:24.780 --> 00:04:27.120
It often runs out before
the end of the day.

00:04:27.120 --> 00:04:29.040
Samsung does that all better.

00:04:29.040 --> 00:04:31.830
It's got two better rear
cameras that snap photos

00:04:31.830 --> 00:04:34.613
instantly, and it has bigger
batteries, one in each

00:04:34.613 --> 00:04:36.390
segment of the phone.

00:04:36.390 --> 00:04:39.290
Samsung only lent me this
phone for 24 hours, though,

00:04:39.290 --> 00:04:41.740
which is not really enough
time for battery testing.

00:04:41.740 --> 00:04:45.470
Is there any way to get in my conclusion?

00:04:45.470 --> 00:04:46.350
- All right, let me just edit this down.

00:04:46.350 --> 00:04:47.300
Hang on one second.

00:04:48.280 --> 00:04:49.765
- All right, let's hear it.

00:04:49.765 --> 00:04:50.639
(phone slaps shut)

00:04:50.639 --> 00:04:51.591
(phone rings)

00:04:51.591 --> 00:04:52.424
(phone slaps shut)

00:04:52.424 --> 00:04:53.257
Cameras.

00:04:53.257 --> 00:04:54.090
(phone slaps shut)

00:04:54.090 --> 00:04:56.590
(phone rings)

00:05:00.460 --> 00:05:02.307
So yes, the Z Flip is the better choice

00:05:02.307 --> 00:05:04.670
of the two, but neither is

00:05:04.670 --> 00:05:06.690
as good as your regular smartphone.

00:05:06.690 --> 00:05:08.720
The technology's getting
better and better though.

00:05:08.720 --> 00:05:10.331
You could say the phone
makers are just starting

00:05:10.331 --> 00:05:13.213
to play the flip phone tune.

00:05:14.770 --> 00:05:17.587
This is my new radio station powered by

00:05:17.587 --> 00:05:19.503
ringtones by Samsung.

00:05:21.030 --> 00:05:23.483
Here's to all those
lovers out there tonight.

